summary:
- topic: Student Representative Report
  text: Student Representative Gabe Domingos provided updates on SOUTHPORTLANDHIGHSCHOOL
    events, athletics, and elementary/middle school activities. He highlighted cultural
    celebrations, sports achievements, and community engagement, concluding with a
    reminder about academic eligibility for extracurriculars.
- topic: School Board Recognition Month
  text: The board members were recognized for School Board Recognition Month, receiving
    unique student artwork themed 'You Belong Here' and new SOUTHPORTLANDSCHOOLDEPARTMENT
    lapel pins. Student artists from SPMS were also honored with certificates for
    their contributions.
- topic: Superintendent's Updates
  text: Superintendent Mr. Matheney reported stable enrollment at 2,933 students and
    discussed the ongoing FY25 budget development process, encouraging community participation
    in upcoming hearings. He also provided updates on school safety initiatives, including
    glass improvements at SOUTHPORTLANDHIGHSCHOOL and the hiring of a new part-time
    security assistant.
- topic: Consent Agenda Approval
  text: The board unanimously approved the consent agenda, which included minutes
    from the previous meeting, the election of Lindsey Hutchins as Behavior Strategist
    for Small School, and the rescission of several outdated policies. Various donations
    from community organizations to different schools were also accepted.
- topic: Policy Approvals
  text: The board approved several policies on their second reading, including Policy
    ADC (Tobacco-Free Schools), Policy JKAA (Use of Physical Restraint and Seclusion),
    Policy JKAA-R (Procedures on Physical Restraint and Seclusion), and Policy GCQC
    (Resignation of School Unit Employees). These policies were largely procedural
    updates based on MaineSchool BoardsAssociation guidance.
- topic: Public Comment on School Boundaries
  text: A citizen urged the board to proactively review extensive materials regarding
    school boundaries and configurations available on the BCSC website. She emphasized
    the importance of this work and encouraged board members to prepare for future
    thoughtful discussions.
